    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d466-a1">

                <pb facs="0650" n="530" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg530"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mrs. Stebbins to
                        Minister Combs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-05-03"><hi rendition="#italic">May 3,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the complaint of my husband,
                    Mr. Al. Stebbins, against ill-treatment and robbery at the hands of one Meleton
                    Agreda, commandante of La Gomera, and my affidavit of February 20 last,
                    confirming same, I beg to inform you that the matter has just been adjusted to
                    my entire satisfaction. As indicated to me in your letter to me of the 18th
                    ultimo, I was called to the office of the minister for foreign affairs
                    yesterday, where I received five promissory notes, each for 1,000 pesos, one
                    payable the 20th instant and one each succeeding month for four months. The
                    notes are signed by Federico Koper &amp; Co., of this city.</p>
                <p>Embracing this opportunity to thank you for your good offices in my behalf,</p>
                <p>I beg, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mrs. Al.
                    Stebbins.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
